# CVEs in upstream base images that cannot be patched at build time.
# Review every base-image bump and remove entries that no longer reproduce.

# ── fluent-bit (fluent/fluent-bit:5.0) ───────────────────────────────────────
# The fluent-bit image ships no shell (/bin/sh absent), so apt-get cannot
# upgrade packages in our Dockerfile. Fix has to come from upstream rebuild.

# libnghttp2-14 — Denial of Service via malformed HTTP/2 frames
CVE-2026-27135

# ── ollama (ollama/ollama:0.23.4) ────────────────────────────────────────────
# CVEs embedded in the upstream /usr/bin/ollama Go binary. We cannot rebuild
# it, so these clear only when ollama publishes a new image with newer Go.

# github.com/buger/jsonparser — DoS via malformed JSON input
CVE-2026-32285

# crypto/x509 — Incorrect enforcement of email constraints
CVE-2026-27137

# net/url — Incorrect parsing of IPv6 host literals
CVE-2026-25679

# crypto/x509, crypto/tls — DoS in certificate chain building
CVE-2026-32280

# crypto/x509 — DoS via inefficient certificate chain validation
CVE-2026-32281

# crypto/tls — DoS via multiple TLS 1.3 key updates
CVE-2026-32283

# crypto/x509 — Certificate validation bypass via incorrect DNS constraint
CVE-2026-33810

# net — LookupCNAME excessive resource consumption with long CNAME chains
CVE-2026-33811

# net/http2 — Infinite loop in HTTP/2 SETTINGS frame processing
CVE-2026-33814

# net/mail — DoS in ParseAddress / ParseAddressList
CVE-2026-39820

# net — Panic in Dial / LookupPort on Windows NUL byte (n/a on Linux runtime)
CVE-2026-39836

# net/mail — DoS via consumePhrase parsing
CVE-2026-42499
